---
/**
 * Inside the LaTeX converter: what follows the scanning stage. Four parts under the same dark roof:
 * the crew (one orchestrator, its subagents and their models), the run (the eight steps), the fidelity
 * marks, and the numbers so far. Facts from the pipeline's own skill files and the two book manifests
 * (5 November 2026). The parts were designed one by one and are composed here; the motion that
 * brings them in is at the end of the style block.
 */
---
<section class="lcx-section section--dark" aria-label="Inside the LaTeX converter" data-lcx>
  <div class="container--wide lcx-stack">
  <div class="lcx lcx-crew">
    <header class="lcx-crew-head">
      <p class="lcx-crew-eyebrow">The crew</p>
      <h3 class="lcx-crew-title"><span>One orchestrator.</span> <span>A crew of subagents.</span></h3>
      <p class="lcx-crew-intro">The orchestrator never transcribes a line. It reads every page, splits the work into blocks, hands each block to a subagent running its own model, compiles what comes back and keeps the state on disk, so a 600-page book advances one chapter at a time and can resume where it stopped.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="lcx-crew-tree">
      <article class="lcx-crew-lead" data-draw aria-labelledby="lcx-crew-r1">
        <div class="lcx-crew-id">
          <h4 class="lcx-crew-role" id="lcx-crew-r1">Orchestrator</h4>
          <p class="lcx-crew-model">Claude Opus&nbsp;5</p>
        </div>
        <p class="lcx-crew-does">Reads every page first and fixes the section hierarchy. Routes the work, compiles, and does the final cross-check against the original.</p>
        <p class="lcx-crew-detail">Up to 5&nbsp;subagents at once.</p>
      </article>

      <ol class="lcx-crew-list" aria-label="Subagents">
        <li class="lcx-crew-card">
          <h4 class="lcx-crew-role">Transcribers</h4>
          <p class="lcx-crew-model">Claude Sonnet&nbsp;5</p>
          <div class="lcx-crew-body">
            <p class="lcx-crew-does">One per block of pages, in two passes with two different prompts: a literal transcript first, then the formatted LaTeX.</p>
            <p class="lcx-crew-detail">The literal is kept. It is what the format pass is audited against.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="lcx-crew-card">
          <h4 class="lcx-crew-role">Figure drawers</h4>
          <p class="lcx-crew-model">Claude Opus&nbsp;5.5</p>
          <div class="lcx-crew-body">
            <p class="lcx-crew-does">One figure per agent. Each diagram is rebuilt in TikZ from measured coordinates and the formula it illustrates, never pasted in as an image.</p>
            <p class="lcx-crew-detail">When Sonnet drew them, 7 of 13&nbsp;figures in one chapter came back wrong. Every one compiled.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="lcx-crew-card">
          <h4 class="lcx-crew-role">Verifier</h4>
          <p class="lcx-crew-model">The orchestrator. Never the transcriber.</p>
          <div class="lcx-crew-body">
            <p class="lcx-crew-does">A model that audits its own work is not an audit. Figures are checked by eye in two passes: content against the original, then overlaps, one figure per page.</p>
            <p class="lcx-crew-detail">Up to 3&nbsp;rounds of compile, render, diff. Then a human looks.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="lcx-crew-card">
          <h4 class="lcx-crew-role">Compiler</h4>
          <p class="lcx-crew-model">pdflatex and a lint script. No model.</p>
          <div class="lcx-crew-body">
            <p class="lcx-crew-does">The lint catches what pdflatex cannot: an empty review note, an orphan figure, a page without its source.</p>
            <p class="lcx-crew-detail">Zero errors, or it does not ship.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <p class="lcx-crew-foot">The orchestrator never needs to see a page, so an open-weights model can take that seat. GLM&nbsp;5.3 is wired in as the free option.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="lcx lcx-run">
    <header class="lcx-run-head">
      <div class="lcx-run-heading">
        <p class="lcx-run-eyebrow">The run</p>
        <h3 class="lcx-run-title" id="run-title">Eight steps. Every one can fail out loud.</h3>
      </div>
      <p class="lcx-run-intro">A check that cannot fail out loud is not a check. Each step has a condition for being done, and the next does not start until it is met.</p>
    </header>

    <ol class="lcx-run-steps" aria-labelledby="run-title">
      <li class="lcx-run-step">
        <h4 class="lcx-run-name">Triage</h4>
        <p class="lcx-run-text">A script decides the route. A PDF with a text layer is extracted with pdftotext, exact and free; a scan or a photo is read by a vision model.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="lcx-run-step">
        <h4 class="lcx-run-name">Index</h4>
        <p class="lcx-run-text">The chapter plan is written to a manifest before anything is transcribed. Every page ends up in a chapter or listed as skipped, with a reason.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="lcx-run-step">
        <h4 class="lcx-run-name">Literal</h4>
        <p class="lcx-run-text">Page by page: the text as it is, the maths in LaTeX, each figure described in one line. An error on the paper is transcribed as an error.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="lcx-run-step">
        <h4 class="lcx-run-name">Format</h4>
        <p class="lcx-run-text">The literal becomes LaTeX in my own style: theorem environments, notation, the density of the prose. Each page opens with a <code class="lcx-run-code">% PÁGINA N</code> marker, so anything can be traced back.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="lcx-run-step">
        <h4 class="lcx-run-name">Figures</h4>
        <p class="lcx-run-text">Every diagram is redrawn in TikZ. A graph is verified against its formula, not against how it looks.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="lcx-run-step">
        <h4 class="lcx-run-name">Lint and compile</h4>
        <p class="lcx-run-text">A lint script, then two passes of pdflatex. The errors are counted with Python, after a shell quirk once reported zero three times in a row.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="lcx-run-step">
        <h4 class="lcx-run-name">Review</h4>
        <p class="lcx-run-text">The orchestrator rereads the result with the original in front of it: signs, subscripts, limits of integration, steps that do not follow.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="lcx-run-step">
        <h4 class="lcx-run-name">Deliver</h4>
        <p class="lcx-run-text">Two PDFs: a clean one to study from, and one that lists every intervention with its page. The original is never overwritten.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="lcx lcx-marks">
    <header class="lcx-marks-head">
      <p class="lcx-marks-eyebrow">Fidelity</p>
      <h3 class="lcx-marks-title" id="lcx-marks-title">Nothing is fixed in silence.</h3>
      <p class="lcx-marks-intro">The paper decides the content; my template decides the form. When the pipeline touches the maths, it leaves a mark, and every mark ends up in a table at the end of the document with the page it came from. One flag in the preamble hides them all for the clean copy.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="lcx-marks-body">
      <!-- The switch: two native radios, visually hidden, drawn as the segmented control below. -->
      <input class="lcx-marks-radio lcx-marks-radio--review" type="radio" name="lcx-marks-mode" id="lcx-marks-review" checked />
      <input class="lcx-marks-radio lcx-marks-radio--clean" type="radio" name="lcx-marks-mode" id="lcx-marks-clean" />

      <dl class="lcx-marks-list">
        <div class="lcx-marks-item lcx-marks-item--used">
          <dt><code><span class="lcx-marks-cmd">\correction</span><span class="lcx-marks-arg">[what was wrong]&#123;…&#125;</span></code></dt>
          <dd>The paper was wrong and this is the fix. Inverted limits, a bad Jacobian, a hypothesis with the wrong sign.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="lcx-marks-item lcx-marks-item--used">
          <dt><code><span class="lcx-marks-cmd">\added</span><span class="lcx-marks-arg">[what was added]&#123;…&#125;</span></code></dt>
          <dd>This was not on the paper: a skipped step, a definition the lecturer took for granted.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="lcx-marks-item">
          <dt><code><span class="lcx-marks-cmd">\review</span></code></dt>
          <dd>A doubt the model could not settle. Someone has to look.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="lcx-marks-item">
          <dt><code><span class="lcx-marks-cmd">\omitted</span></code></dt>
          <dd>Left out on purpose, and said so. Never in silence.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>

      <figure class="lcx-marks-demo">
        <div class="lcx-marks-seg"><span class="lcx-marks-thumb" aria-hidden="true"></span><label class="lcx-marks-opt lcx-marks-opt--review" for="lcx-marks-review">Review</label><label class="lcx-marks-opt lcx-marks-opt--clean" for="lcx-marks-clean">Clean</label></div>

        <div class="lcx-marks-tile">
          <pre class="lcx-marks-code"><code><span class="lcx-marks-ln"><span class="lcx-marks-kw">\usepackage</span><span class="lcx-marks-flag">[entrega]</span>&#123;apuntes-nmg&#125;</span>
  <span class="lcx-marks-ln"> </span>
  <span class="lcx-marks-ln"><span class="lcx-marks-kw">\begin</span>&#123;theorem&#125;[Change of variables]</span>
  <span class="lcx-marks-ln">  \[ \int_V f(y)\,dy</span>
  <span class="lcx-marks-ln">     = \int_U f(\varphi(x))\,<span class="lcx-marks-mk"><span class="lcx-marks-mk-cmd">\correction</span><span class="lcx-marks-mk-note">[absolute value was missing]</span>&#123;</span>\lvert\det D\varphi(x)\rvert<span class="lcx-marks-mk">&#125;</span>\,dx \]</span>
  <span class="lcx-marks-ln"><span class="lcx-marks-kw">\end</span>&#123;theorem&#125;</span>
  <span class="lcx-marks-ln"><span class="lcx-marks-mk"><span class="lcx-marks-mk-cmd">\added</span><span class="lcx-marks-mk-note">[step skipped in the notebook]</span>&#123;</span>Since $\varphi$ is a diffeomorphism, $\det D\varphi \neq 0$.<span class="lcx-marks-mk">&#125;</span></span></code></pre>

          <div class="lcx-marks-page" aria-label="The same lines, compiled">
            <div class="lcx-marks-row">
              <div class="lcx-marks-text">
                <p><b>Theorem 1</b> (Change of variables)<b>.</b></p>
                <math display="block">
                  <msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>V</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mspace width="0.17em" /><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi>
                  <mo>=</mo>
                  <msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>U</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mspace width="0.17em" />
                  <mrow class="lcx-marks-fix"><mo form="prefix" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>det</mi><mspace width="0.17em" /><mi>D</mi><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo form="postfix" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mspace width="0.17em" /><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi>
                </math>
              </div>
              <p class="lcx-marks-note">absolute value was missing</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lcx-marks-row">
              <p class="lcx-marks-text lcx-marks-add">Since <math><mi>φ</mi></math> is a diffeomorphism, <math><mi>det</mi><mspace width="0.17em" /><mi>D</mi><mi>φ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>
              <p class="lcx-marks-note">step skipped in the notebook</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <figcaption class="lcx-marks-cap">
          <span class="lcx-marks-cap--review"><code>\usepackage&#123;apuntes-nmg&#125;</code> shows the marks and the table.</span>
          <span class="lcx-marks-cap--clean"><code>\usepackage[entrega]&#123;apuntes-nmg&#125;</code> hides them: the clean copy.</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="lcx lcx-numbers">
    <h3 class="lcx-numbers-title">So far</h3>
    <dl class="lcx-numbers-row">
      <div class="lcx-numbers-stat"><dt class="lcx-numbers-label">pages compiled</dt><dd class="lcx-numbers-value">969</dd></div>
      <div class="lcx-numbers-stat"><dt class="lcx-numbers-label">figures redrawn in TikZ</dt><dd class="lcx-numbers-value">624</dd></div>
      <div class="lcx-numbers-stat"><dt class="lcx-numbers-label">chapters, plus appendices</dt><dd class="lcx-numbers-value">27</dd></div>
      <div class="lcx-numbers-stat"><dt class="lcx-numbers-label">compile errors at delivery</dt><dd class="lcx-numbers-value">0</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .lcx-section { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem) clamp(5rem, 11vw, 10rem); }
  .lcx-stack { display: grid; gap: clamp(5rem, 9vw, 8rem); }
  .lcx-crew { padding-block: 0; }

  /* ===== crew ===== */
  /* The crew: one row above, four below, joined by hairlines. The structure is the diagram. */
  .lcx-crew {
    --lcx-crew-gap: clamp(1.5rem, 2.6vw, 2.5rem);
    --lcx-crew-line: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    --lcx-crew-drop: 2.5rem;
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    color: var(--on-dark);
  }

  /* Header */
  .lcx-crew-head { display: grid; gap: 0.75rem; max-width: 40rem; margin-bottom: clamp(3rem, 5vw, 4.5rem); }
  .lcx-crew-eyebrow {
    font-size: clamp(1.1875rem, 1.6vw, 1.5rem); line-height: 1.17; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.009em;
    color: var(--on-dark-2);
  }
  .lcx-crew-title {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 3vw, 2.75rem); line-height: 1.06; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .lcx-crew-title span { white-space: nowrap; }
  .lcx-crew-intro {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.47; letter-spacing: 0;
    color: var(--on-dark-2); text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  /* Shared card type */
  .lcx-crew-role {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.1875rem; line-height: 1.21; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.009em;
  }
  .lcx-crew-model {
    margin-top: 0.375rem;
    font: 400 0.8125rem/1.38 var(--mono); letter-spacing: 0;
    color: var(--on-dark-2);
  }
  .lcx-crew-does {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.4; letter-spacing: 0.005em;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .lcx-crew-detail {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.43; letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    color: var(--on-dark-2); text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  /* The orchestrator: spans the width, on the same four-column grid as the crew below. */
  .lcx-crew-lead {
    position: relative;
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); column-gap: var(--lcx-crew-gap);
    align-items: baseline;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--link-on-dark);
  }
  .lcx-crew-lead .lcx-crew-id { grid-column: 1; }
  .lcx-crew-lead .lcx-crew-role { font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.17; letter-spacing: -0.005em; }
  .lcx-crew-lead .lcx-crew-does { grid-column: 2 / span 2; margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.47; letter-spacing: 0; }
  .lcx-crew-lead .lcx-crew-detail { grid-column: 4; margin-top: 0; }
  /* The stem: from the orchestrator down to the bus. */
  .lcx-crew-lead::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: calc(100% + 0.75rem);
    width: 1px; height: calc(var(--lcx-crew-drop) - 0.75rem);
    background: var(--lcx-crew-line);
  }

  /* The crew */
  .lcx-crew-list {
    position: relative;
    list-style: none; margin: var(--lcx-crew-drop) 0 0; padding: 0;
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); column-gap: var(--lcx-crew-gap);
    grid-auto-rows: auto;
  }
  /* The bus: from the stem to the last column. */
  .lcx-crew-list::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0;
    right: calc((100% - 3 * var(--lcx-crew-gap)) / 4);
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--lcx-crew-line);
  }
  .lcx-crew-card {
    position: relative; padding-top: 1.75rem;
    /* Role, model, body line up across the columns: a model that wraps pushes every card's body down together. */
    display: grid; grid-row: span 3; grid-template-rows: subgrid; row-gap: 0; align-content: start;
  }
  /* Each drop: from the bus into the card. */
  .lcx-crew-card::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0;
    width: 1px; height: 1rem;
    background: var(--lcx-crew-line);
  }

  .lcx-crew-foot {
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
    font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.43; letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    color: var(--on-dark-2); text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  /* Narrower desktops: the crew goes two by two; the orchestrator keeps the width. */
  @media (max-width: 1080px) {
    .lcx-crew-lead { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); row-gap: 1rem; }
    .lcx-crew-lead .lcx-crew-id { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
    .lcx-crew-lead .lcx-crew-does { grid-column: 1; }
    .lcx-crew-lead .lcx-crew-detail { grid-column: 2; }
    .lcx-crew-list { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .lcx-crew-card:nth-child(n + 3) { margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: 0; }
    .lcx-crew-card:nth-child(n + 3)::before { display: none; }
    .lcx-crew-list::before { right: calc((100% - var(--lcx-crew-gap)) / 2); }
  }

  /* Phones: one column, the hairline runs down the left and ticks out to each role. */
  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .lcx-crew { --lcx-crew-drop: 1.5rem; }
    .lcx-crew-lead { display: block; padding-top: 1rem; }
    .lcx-crew-lead .lcx-crew-role { font-size: 1.3125rem; }
    .lcx-crew-lead .lcx-crew-does { margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.4; letter-spacing: 0.005em; }
    .lcx-crew-lead .lcx-crew-detail { margin-top: 0.75rem; }
    .lcx-crew-list { display: block; margin-top: 0; padding-top: var(--lcx-crew-drop); }
    .lcx-crew-list::before { display: none; }
    .lcx-crew-lead::after { display: none; }
    /* The spine: each card carries its own stretch of it; the last one stops at its tick. */
    .lcx-crew-card, .lcx-crew-card:nth-child(n + 3) { display: block; margin-top: 0; padding: 0 0 2.25rem 1.5rem; }
    .lcx-crew-card:last-child { padding-bottom: 0; }
    .lcx-crew-card::before, .lcx-crew-card:nth-child(n + 3)::before { display: block; top: 0.6875rem; width: 1rem; height: 1px; }
    .lcx-crew-card::after {
      content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: calc(0.75rem - var(--lcx-crew-drop)); bottom: 0;
      width: 1px; background: var(--lcx-crew-line);
    }
    .lcx-crew-card + .lcx-crew-card::after { top: 0; }
    .lcx-crew-card:last-child::after { bottom: auto; height: calc(var(--lcx-crew-drop) - 0.0625rem); }
    .lcx-crew-card + .lcx-crew-card:last-child::after { height: 0.75rem; }
  }

  /* ===== run ===== */
  /* The run: the long form of the stage's legend. Same hairline, same mono counter, same two greys;
     each step gains a name and its done-condition. */
  .lcx-run {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 4.5vw, 4rem);
  }

  /* Head: on the same two columns as the steps, so the intro sits over steps 5 to 8. */
  .lcx-run-head {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    column-gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 5rem);
    align-items: end;
  }
  .lcx-run-heading { display: grid; gap: 0.75rem; }
  .lcx-run-eyebrow {
    font-size: 1.1875rem; line-height: 1.17; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.009em;
    color: var(--on-dark-2);
  }
  .lcx-run-title {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 3vw, 2.75rem); line-height: 1.06; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--on-dark);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .lcx-run-intro {
    max-width: 32rem;
    font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.47; letter-spacing: 0;
    color: var(--on-dark-2);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  /* Steps: 1 to 4 run down the left column, 5 to 8 down the right; rows are shared, so the numbers
     line up across. */
  .lcx-run-steps {
    list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0;
    counter-reset: lcx-run;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    grid-template-rows: repeat(4, auto);
    grid-auto-flow: column;
    column-gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 5rem);
  }
  .lcx-run-step {
    counter-increment: lcx-run;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.5rem 1.25rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    grid-template-rows: auto 1fr;
    align-items: baseline;
    row-gap: 0.25rem;
    padding-block: 2rem 0;
  }
  .lcx-run-step:nth-child(1), .lcx-run-step:nth-child(5) { padding-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12); }
  .lcx-run-step::before {
    content: '';
    grid-column: 1; grid-row: 1; align-self: center;
    width: 1rem; height: 1px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.24);
  }
  .lcx-run-step::after {
    content: counter(lcx-run);
    grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1;
    font: 400 0.8125rem/1 var(--mono);
    color: var(--on-dark-2);
  }
  .lcx-run-name {
    grid-column: 3; grid-row: 1;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.1875rem; line-height: 1.21; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--on-dark);
  }
  .lcx-run-text {
    grid-column: 3; grid-row: 2;
    max-width: 32rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.4; letter-spacing: 0.005em;
    color: var(--on-dark-2);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .lcx-run-code {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.875em; letter-spacing: 0;
